From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sheepsticked <72666364+Sheepsticked@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] an unexpected ERROR no longer crashes Asterisk

Upstream: https://github.com/IchthysMaranatha/asterisk-chan-quectel @ 3d45c7f072131296a7e3c1a4faf5bb18751dbd87
Purpose: at_response_error() logs an ERROR, +CME ERROR or +CMS ERROR that
         arrives while the command queue is empty through
         log_cmd_response_error(), which read the flags of the missing
         command: a NULL dereference that ended Asterisk with SIGSEGV
         (applies on top of 0012)

Such an error comes from a late answer after the driver gave up waiting
and reconnected, or from a modem that sends an extra error. It is now
logged as "Received unexpected 'ERROR'" like the other unexpected results.
---
 at_response.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/at_response.c b/at_response.c
index bb96a50..68740ed 100644
--- a/at_response.c
+++ b/at_response.c
@@ -448,7 +448,8 @@ static void log_cmd_response_error(const struct pvt* pvt, const at_queue_cmd_t *
 	va_list ap;
 	char tempbuff[512];
 
-	if (at_cmd_suppress_error_mode(ecmd->flags) == SUPPRESS_ERROR_ENABLED) {
+	/* an error with no command waiting for it (a late or extra answer) has no flags to read */
+	if (ecmd && at_cmd_suppress_error_mode(ecmd->flags) == SUPPRESS_ERROR_ENABLED) {
 		if (DEBUG_ATLEAST(1)) {
 			ast_log(AST_LOG_DEBUG, "[%s] Command response error suppressed:\n", PVT_ID(pvt));
 			va_start(ap, fmt);
